.TH INSTALLPKG 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
installpkg \- controlled exact-NVR live-system installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B installpkg
.I PACKAGE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B installpkg
installs exactly one package on the live system at the newest NVR
carried by the live generation index. A bare
.I apk add name
is a no-op when any version is installed, so the atom is pinned
explicitly and the installed version is verified to be the intended
NVR afterwards; local publication is authoritative, with no apksync
coupling. This is one of the two privileged admin boundaries (with
.BR sign-apk-repo (8));
.BR makepkg (1)
is the sole APK constructor and never installs.
.PP
Exact installs record their constraint in the package world; prefer
bare names afterwards unless a hold is intended, or the next upgrade
will silently skip the package.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the package name. Must be run
as root; use sudo explicitly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apk/world
Wanted-package list (exact pins held here show up on upgrade).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Installed the intended NVR.
.TP
.B 1
Missing index, absent package, version mismatch, or not root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo installpkg nginx
.RE
